  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Transitive use with «avere»",
     "texto": [
      "When the verb has a direct object (it answers «what?»): use **avere**. The past participle ends in **-o**: **Ho cambiato lavoro** (I changed jobs), **Ho finito il libro** (I finished the book), **Abbiamo cominciato la lezione** (we started the class)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Intransitive use with «essere»",
     "texto": [
      "When there's no direct object and the subject itself is the one changing state or finishing: use **essere** with compulsory agreement: **La situazione è cambiata** (the situation has changed), **Il film è finito tardi** (the film finished late), **La lezione è cominciata alle nove** (the class started at nine)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Transitive (with avere) versus intransitive (with essere)",
     "columnas": [
      {
       "texto": "Transitive (direct object)",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Intransitive (the subject changes)",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      }
     ],
